ime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_011SwRQUitDNdCAeyus7FH9G", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 52932, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_011SwRQUitDNdCAeyus7FH9G", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 54520, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_016FKrooopRYQaam8QSzr8V5", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 54820, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_016FKrooopRYQaam8QSzr8V5", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 54820, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_016FKrooopRYQaam8QSzr8V5", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 59018, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, its most recent healthy release, in all regions. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged the on-call engineer.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with about 18% of requests erroring. The previous attempt, v2.3.1-rc, was also unhealthy, so I went back to v2.3.0. The first rollback stopped partway with an orchestrator error after updating only us-east. The other two regions were still on v2.3.1, so I retried once and it finished. All three regions now run v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is down to about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The request to create INC-0001 timed out. I checked the incident list before retrying and found it had been created, so there's only one incident and one page. It covers what happened, the stalled first rollback, and two follow-ups: find out why v2.3.1 fails, and look into the orchestrator error.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01HNjeCxVAfToMjNxEot1ujc", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01PChFvXGKrWtp292Q7siwZh", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01LtvNban4kmAftg8PsSwwqP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_0171hj5PwStmCeMBoQ6hF5QP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Rollback stopped partway. Only us-east is on v2.3.0. A rollback to a known-healthy version is safe to repeat, so I'll retry it once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01FaoSJjPSBXsnCUgPSSYpAE", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_018RKgnxZLHoP69rEQZsXanp", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_015icviWsFM3MQLxcSFUrz2A", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_011SwRQUitDNdCAeyus7FH9G", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest deploy) was failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1-rc was also marked unhealthy. I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. The first rollback attempt partially failed: an orchestrator error stopped the rollout after us-east, leaving the service on mixed versions. A retry finished the rollout. All three regions are now on v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The request timed out, so I'll check whether the incident was created before retrying. A duplicate would page on-call twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_016FKrooopRYQaam8QSzr8V5", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, its most recent healthy release, in all regions. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged the on-call engineer.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with about 18% of requests erroring. The previous attempt, v2.3.1-rc, was also unhealthy, so I went back to v2.3.0. The first rollback stopped partway with an orchestrator error after updating only us-east. The other two regions were still on v2.3.1, so I retried once and it finished. All three regions now run v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is down to about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The request to create INC-0001 timed out. I checked the incident list before retrying and found it had been created, so there's only one incident and one page. It covers what happened, the stalled first rollback, and two follow-ups: find out why v2.3.1 fails, and look into the orchestrator error.", "type": "text"}]}]}